=========================================================================
BUILD CHECKLIST (new leather, kilim, or wood piece)
=========================================================================
1. productSet (synchronous:true): Size=[...one or more...],
   Construction=[Leather|Kilim|Wood], one variant PER size, CONTINUE, price(s).
   Tags include category + material + 'Made to Order'.
2. metafieldsSet: aav.configurator (Template A/B/C/D), aav.swatches (leather/
   hardware/legs/handle IDs as the family needs), aav.size_dimensions (ONE KEY
   PER SIZE VALUE), and aav.wood_finishes if the piece has a Wood Finish picker.
   Confirm unit_map keys == size_dimensions keys == size option values.
   For full-range leather, list all 10 canonical IDs of the RIGHT library —
   'Leather' for upholstery pieces, 'Furniture Leather' for hard furniture
   (propagation rule, #2 gotcha).
3. Upload photos; set alt text per aa-alt-text-convention; publish (ACTIVE) + add
   to relevant collection (tag-based smart collection).
4. AFTER any later change to a shared swatch library, re-run the audit query and
   append new IDs to every product that should carry them (propagation rule).

=========================================================================
HANDLE-FINISH INHERITANCE — picker options that mirror another picker
=========================================================================
OPT-IN, DORMANT BY DEFAULT. A picker may declare an "inherit" map so that
chosen options take their colour/photo FROM ANOTHER PICKER's current selection
instead of their own seeded swatch. Used on the chest Handles picker so the
metal handles always match the chosen Metal Finish, and the leather handle
always matches the body leather. Products without an "inherit" key are wholly
unaffected — the engine no-ops when the key is absent.

SCHEMA — add "inherit" to the inheriting picker only:
  {"key":"handle","label":"Handles","category":"Handle","property":"Handles",
   "order_swatch":false,
   "inherit":{"Metal Knobs":"hardware","Metal Handles":"hardware",
              "Leather Handles":"leather"}}
  - KEY  = the option's swatch NAME, byte-for-byte (must match the metaobject
           'name' exactly, including case + spacing).
  - VALUE = the picker KEY it inherits from (e.g. "hardware", "leather").
  An option NOT listed in the map keeps its own seeded swatch as normal.

BEHAVIOUR:
  - Selected row: when an inheriting option is chosen, its dot + name + cart
    property mirror the source picker's current selection, e.g. the cart
    property reads  Handles: Metal Handles (Silver).
  - Open-picker OPTIONS: when you open the Handles picker after choosing a
    metal finish, the metal-handle OPTION CHIPS render IN that finish (Silver),
    not their seeded brass. Change the finish and reopen — the chips update.
  - Leather Handles chip mirrors the chosen body leather colour the same way.

WHY IT'S WIRED THE WAY IT IS (two-part fix — keep BOTH):
  1) resolveInheritedItems(pk, items) clones each inheriting option and
     overwrites its hex/img from the source picker's current selection BEFORE
     registerPicker() hands the items to the modal. The modal paints option
     chips from the items array it is given at register() time (cell colour =
     it.img || it.hex), so the items must be repainted BEFORE registration —
     not after.
  2) syncInheritors(changedKey) re-registers an inheriting picker whenever the
     SOURCE changes. The trigger is driven by the inherit MAP (does ANY of this
     picker's options inherit from changedKey — via inheritDependsOn), NOT by
     which option is currently selected.

  *** THE BUG THAT COST THREE DEPLOYS — READ THIS ***
  The first attempts re-registered the Handles picker only when its CURRENTLY
  SELECTED option inherited from the changed source. But the default handle
  selection is "Leather Handles", which inherits from leather — so changing the
  Metal Finish hit a guard that said "selected option doesn't depend on
  hardware" and skipped the repaint entirely. The metal OPTION chips never
  updated and kept showing seeded brass. FIX: gate on the inherit MAP's VALUES
  (any option depends on the changed source), never on the current selection.
  GENERAL LESSON: when the SAME code shows DIFFERENT behaviour, suspect a DATA
  difference; and when stuck after two guesses, REPRODUCE the engine logic in a
  tiny Node harness with the REAL swatch/configurator JSON rather than reasoning
  from the rendered screen. The harness found it in seconds.

  ALSO REMEMBER: the modal renders OPTIONS from the items array passed at
  register() time. To change how options LOOK you must rewrite items before
  register() AND re-register when the source changes — repainting only the
  selected row is not enough.

REQUIREMENTS / GOTCHAS:
  - Option NAMES in the map must byte-match the swatch metaobject names. A typo
    silently no-ops (looks like "inheritance isn't working").
  - Source pickers must be listed in cfg.pickers (e.g. "hardware", "leather")
    and their swatch IDs present in aav.swatches.
  - Inheritance is colour/photo only — it does NOT add a price/surcharge and
    does NOT create variants. Cart property records "Option (Source)".
  - Metal finishes are currently HEX-ONLY chips; they read as plausible metal
    tones. When real finish photos are added to the swatch 'photo' field, the
    inherited chips use the photo automatically — no code change.

LIVE ON: Chest of Drawers — Leather (8322681634863) and — Kilim (8322681700399).
Both configs already carry the inherit map; the wood + cane chests do not (no
handles inheriting a finish), and are unaffected.

